---
source: crates/agtrace-cli/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: help
---
Monitor live agents in real-time.

Shows the sessions of the current project (Claude Code and Codex), live ones
first, each with its agent tree: teammates, subagents, forks and Codex child
threads. A navigator on the left lists the scope, its sessions and their agents
(finished ones fold into one node, d shows them in place); the right side shows
the selected node (the overview, a session, an agent's detail) above the messages
scoped to it. Up/Down move, Right/Left expand and collapse or walk the
hierarchy, Enter reads the selection. Press ? in the TUI for key bindings.

By default, sessions whose log changed within --since (2h) or whose Claude process
is still running are shown. Use --session to watch one session tree.

Usage: agtrace watch [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --session <ID>
          Watch one session tree (session id or prefix from the index, or an agent id such as codex:<thread>)

      --since <SINCE>
          Include root sessions active within this window (e.g. 30m, 2h, 1d)
          
          [default: 2h]

      --mode <MODE>
          Display mode: tui (interactive) or console (line output for non-TTY / CI)
          
          [default: tui]
          [possible values: tui, console]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global Options:
      --data-dir <DATA_DIR>
          Directory for agtrace database and configuration (defaults to system data directory, or AGTRACE_PATH env var)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format for command results
          
          [default: plain]
          [possible values: plain, json]

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Logging verbosity level
          
          [default: info]
          [possible values: error, warn, info, debug, trace]

      --project <PROJECT_ROOT>
          Target project directory (defaults to current directory)

      --all-projects
          Operate on all indexed projects instead of current project only

      --all-worktrees
          Include sessions from all git worktrees of the current repository
